 The output visualization of gs point clouds and estimated_transform.npz will be saved under 'demo_outputs'. 
 
+### 1.5 Offset Benchmark (mixed trials + SLURM-ready)
+
+We provide a benchmark runner at `scripts/run_gaussreg_offsets.sh` that:
+- randomizes ref/src Gaussian pairs,
+- runs GaussReg (`demo.py`),
+- saves transformed PLYs, logs, and estimated transforms,
+- writes a single `results.csv` with run metadata and output paths.
+
+Default schedule per pair:
+- `50` trials in `xyz_only` mode (fast; only xyz transformed),
+- `10` trials in `full_features` mode (xyz + quaternion/SH updates).
+
+Run locally:
+```bash
+./scripts/run_gaussreg_offsets.sh \
+  --data-root /path/to/trained_gaussians \
+  --weights weights/coarse_registration.pth.tar
+```
+
+Key options:
+```bash
+--xyz-trials <int>      # default 50
+--full-trials <int>     # default 10
+--max-translation 500
+--max-rotation-deg 180
+--heartbeat-sec 30      # progress prints while demo is running
+```
+
+SLURM array usage (scene sharding):
+```bash
+sbatch --array=0-3 --gres=gpu:1 --cpus-per-task=8 --mem=32G --time=24:00:00 \
+  --wrap="cd /path/to/GaussReg && ./scripts/run_gaussreg_offsets.sh \
+    --data-root /path/to/trained_gaussians \
+    --weights weights/coarse_registration.pth.tar \
+    --shard-index \${SLURM_ARRAY_TASK_ID} \
+    --num-shards 4"
+```
+
+Notes:
+- Each CSV row includes `trial_mode`, `xyz_only_mode`, and `rotate_sh_mode`.
+- In SLURM, output folder names include job/array ids by default for easier tracking.
+
